{
  "sn16.7:0.1": "Linked Discourses 16.7 ",
  "sn16.7:0.2": "1. Kassapa ",
  "sn16.7:0.3": "Advice (2nd) ",
  "sn16.7:1.1": "Near Rājagaha, in the Bamboo Grove. ",
  "sn16.7:1.2": "Then Venerable Mahākassapa went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. ",
  "sn16.7:1.3": "The Buddha said to him, ",
  "sn16.7:1.4": "“Kassapa, advise the mendicants! ",
  "sn16.7:1.5": "Give them a Dhamma talk! ",
  "sn16.7:1.6": "Either you or I should advise the mendicants ",
  "sn16.7:1.7": "and give them a Dhamma talk.” ",
  "sn16.7:2.1": "“Sir, the mendicants these days are hard to admonish, having qualities that make them hard to admonish. They’re impatient, and don’t take instruction respectfully. ",
  "sn16.7:2.2": "Sir, whoever has no faith, conscience, prudence, energy, and wisdom when it comes to skillful qualities can expect decline, not growth, in skillful qualities, whether by day or by night. ",
  "sn16.7:3.1": "It’s like the moon in the waning fortnight. Whether by day or by night, its beauty, roundness, luminosity, and diameter and circumference only decline. ",
  "sn16.7:3.2": "In the same way, whoever has no faith, conscience, prudence, energy, and wisdom when it comes to skillful qualities can expect decline, not growth, in skillful qualities, whether by day or by night. ",
  "sn16.7:3.3": "",
  "sn16.7:3.4": "",
  "sn16.7:3.5": "",
  "sn16.7:3.6": "",
  "sn16.7:4.1": "A faithless individual is in decline. ",
  "sn16.7:4.2": "An individual with no conscience is in decline. ",
  "sn16.7